      "fine_trace_step": 3,
      "description": "Root cause. `X86_get_insn_id()` writes the public instruction id only on a successful table lookup. For the exact witness path, the internal opcode exists in the X86 opcode enum but has no vulnerable `insns[]` entry, so `find_insn()` misses and this function leaves the heap `cs_insn.id` from `cs_disasm()` uninitialized."
